      "id": "05-15",
      "title": "A numerical distance-vector update",
      "chapter": "From algorithm to routers",
      "duration": 20.3,
      "narration": "B advertises ten to F, giving A fourteen through B. C advertises eleven, giving thirteen through C. A chooses the lower candidate and installs C as next hop.",
      "bullets": [
        "Via B: 4 + 10 = 14",
        "Via C: 2 + 11 = 13"
      ],
      "takeaway": "The Bellman-Ford update combines a local link cost with a neighbor estimate.",
